From 1b608e08ebd0e87e339595e84562785a1b1ca5ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:43:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(auth): scope read-only pool parsing to picker builds
 [daveey]

Keep every read-modify-write loader fresh. Revalidate the active auth file on every scoped pool read, deep-copy returned slices, and discard scope data on exit. Bind parsing to the sampled path; copied contexts cannot reuse snapshots on another thread or after exit.

Proof so far: initial parse-count test RED (2 loads instead of 1), sampled-path race RED then fixed; 123 focused consumer tests GREEN, then 13 expanded scope tests GREEN; scripts/check all 20 gates GREEN. Intermediate review found sampled-path race, fixed with deterministic regression. Hub diagnostic A/B measured ~5-7ms reduction of ~69ms warm model.options with zero auth-write attempts; async usage payload changes still need controlled parity proof. Not yet final acceptance, reviewed for landing, or deployed.
